FIVE LAMPS — WHY DIWALI IS CELEBRATED
A shadow puppet film for Narratude.

Third-party assets used in the film
- Narration voice: Kokoro TTS v1.0 (kokoro-onnx), voice "af_heart" — model and voices under the Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx · https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
- Typeface: Cormorant Garamond (Christian Thalmann / Catharsis Fonts) — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt)
  https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/cormorantgaramond
- Music samples (CC0 1.0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios) — flute (bansuri line), oboe (shehnai line)
  https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE

Made in code, no third-party assets
- All puppets, scenery, carving patterns, plaques, the Lamp Rail and the stage were drawn procedurally in code for this film.
- Percussion (dholak, manjira, ghungroo, temple bells), the tanpura drone and all sound effects were synthesised in numpy;
  the plucked string uses physical modelling (Karplus–Strong). All melodies are original.
- Rendering and mixing tools: the Lemo-Opuscar toolkit (MIT licence).

Stories: traditional and public-domain religious narratives (Ramayana; Samudra Manthan; Krishna and Narakasura;
Bandi Chhor Divas; the nirvana of Mahavira). No existing artwork, puppet, recording or melody was copied.
